  "subtitle": "[ASSET: left | ComeOnChick | width=12%] [ASSET: right | MabelAndZelda | width=12%] This month's VMA goes to [LINK:1963:ASM_4|ASM #4] where Flash Thompson says to Liz Allan \"Come on, chick!&nbsp; Let's go!\"\n[BR]\n[BR] Though Sue Storm's brush with two ladies at the department store named \"Mabel\" and \"Zelda\" in [LINK:1963:FF_18|FF #18] deserves an Honorable Mention shout-out as well!",
  "review_text": "The seven graded stories this month (an extra one due to the <i>Strange Tales </i>annual) resulted in a weighted average of [SPAN: severity=error; fontsize=large; fonttype=bold; text=x.xx], nearly a full point better than the previous month and yet <i>hardly</i> setting the world on fire.\n\nThor hasn't hit any kind of stride yet, Ant-Man continues to be bad just about every month, the Human Torch solo features are not making anyone yearn for the next issue, and even the promising Iron Man hasn't been given much to do yet, consistently making the <i>Journey Into Strange Tales of Suspense to Astonish</i> books the low points of each month.&nbsp; The FF, while certainly not <i>bad</i>, didn't really bring the goods this month.&nbsp; Only the Amazing Spider-Man was genuinely excellent this time around, complete with the welcome news that it will now be published monthly!\n\n\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** SUMMARY_BEGIN ***\n*** THIS MONTH ***7 graded stories over 7 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 5 grade character issue       weight 7.5   asm       ASM #4      1.00 5.0   iron      TOS #45     0.75 4.5   ff        FF #18      1.00 4.5   torch     ST #112     0.50 3.5   torch     ST Annual 2 0.75 2.5   ant       TTA #47     0.50 2.0   thor      JIM #95     0.504.58*** LAST MONTH ***6 graded stories over 5 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 3.25 grade character issue   weight 3.5   ff        FF #17  1.00 3.5   strange   ST #111 0.25 3.0   torch     ST #111 0.50 2.5   ant       TTA #46 0.50 2.5   iron      TOS #44 0.50 1.5   thor      JIM #94 0.502.81\n*** SUMMARY_END ***]",
  "letters_page": "[HANG0] * Introduction of Sandman, Super-Skrull, Betty Brant, Happy Hogan and Pepper Potts\n[HANG0] * A full-length early Marvel Team-Up with the Human Torch and Spider-Man sharing more than just a couple of pages this time\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** INTRODUCTION_BEGIN ***\nNotes | first | villain | death | Professor Lawrence Zaxton\nNotes | first | villain | Liso Trago\nBetty Brant | Milestone: (first)\nSandman | villain | Milestone: (first), (origin)\nEmperor Dorrek VII | villain | unnamed | Milestone: (first)\nSuper-Skrull | villain | Milestone: (first)\nNotes | first | villain | The Fox (Reynard Slinker)\nEel | villain | Milestone: (first)\nHappy Hogan | Milestone: (first)\nJack Frost | villain | Milestone: (first), (origin)\nPepper Potts | Milestone: (first)\n*** INTRODUCTION_END ***]\n\n<b>Roundup:</b>\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_BEGIN ***]\n[HANG0] * Thor's adventure doubles down on duplication -- and on a brand of absurdity fit for 1963 or a 5<sup>th</sup>-dimension prankster.\n[HANG0] * Trago toots, Ant‑Man and the Wasp flail, and the backup story does all the heavy lifting.\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * The shiny new toy of the Super‑Skrull meets the Fantastic Four in a story that struggles to escape its Atlas roots.\n[HANG0] * Spider‑Man and the Human Torch finally get a full‑length clash, but Longbox Playback's first Annual forgets to bring a plot.\n[HANG0] * A flimsy Human Torch tale held together by sheer enthusiasm, a dash of altruism, and the kind of Silver Age audacity that somehow makes the whole thing work.\n[HANG0] * Cold villain, lukewarm adventure, but Iron Man's world finally starts to thaw into shape.\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_END ***]",
  "ownership": "In what promises to be a <i>huge</i> month, with 9 books upcoming:\n[HANG0] * the FF are on call <i>twice</i> this month, having to face both the Sub-Mariner and a threat from ancient Egypt to boot\n[HANG0] * and speaking of blasts from the past, Thor faces off against Merlin!\n[HANG0] * Dr. Doom drops in on Spider-Man\n[HANG0] * Ant-Man and the Wasp take on a spiny new menace\n[HANG0] * Torchy has a new girlfriend\n[HANG0] * Iron Man takes on another \"red\" menace\n\nAnd finally, as if writing annuals wasn't enough, Marvel kicks off the second half of 1963 with two <i>new </i>books in the form of <i>Avengers</i> and <i>X-Men</i>!\n\nHold onto your hats, folks.&nbsp; It looks like a busy month!"
}